+/*!
+ * \brief Realigning a subtitle on the video's speech, for a video whose own subtitles cannot tell
+ * how to lay it.
+ *
+ * Where someone speaks is read from the sound, a chance for every 32 ms, by Silero's voice
+ * activity model (MIT licence, its weights shipped in an add-on). The subtitle shows a line
+ * where someone speaks and nothing in the silences between, so the change to its times that
+ * best lays its lines on the speech - an offset, and a known frame-rate ratio - is the one that
+ * puts most speech under lines and least under nothing. A line that translates something written
+ * on screen moves with the rest.
+ *
